### Task Management Features - Test Script
### Use this file to test all task features after deployment

### Variables
@baseUrl = https://your-api.azurewebsites.net/api/v1
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@userId = YOUR_USER_ID_HERE
@taskId = TASK_ID_WILL_BE_SET_AFTER_CREATION

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE TASK - Unassigned (This was failing before)
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Unassigned Task",
  "description": "This task has no assignee - testing the fix",
  "priority": "High",
  "category": "Development",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": 5.0,
  "tags": "test,unassigned,fix"
}

### Expected: 201 Created
### Copy the task ID from response and set @taskId variable above

### ============================================
### 2. CREATE TASK - Assigned
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Assigned Task",
  "description": "This task has an assignee",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "category": "Design",
  "assignedToUserId": "{{userId}}",
  "dueDate": "2026-06-15T12:00:00Z",
  "estimatedHours": 3.0,
  "tags": "test,assigned"
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### ============================================
### 3. GET ALL TASKS
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with list of tasks

### ============================================
### 4. GET TASK BY ID
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with task details
### Should show "assignedTo": null for unassigned tasks

### ============================================
### 5. UPDATE TASK
### ============================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Task Title",
  "description": "Updated description",
  "priority": "Critical",
  "category": "Operations",
  "status": "InProgress",
  "assignedToUserId": "{{userId}}",
  "dueDate": "2026-06-20T12:00:00Z",
  "estimatedHours": 8.0,
  "actualHours": 2.0,
  "tags": "test,updated"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with updated task

### ============================================
### 6. UPDATE TASK STATUS
### ============================================
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Completed"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with updated task

### ============================================
### 7. ADD COMMENT
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test comment to verify the feature works!"
}

### Expected: 201 Created with comment details
### Copy comment ID for next test

### ============================================
### 8. GET COMMENTS
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with list of comments

### ============================================
### 9. DELETE COMMENT
### ============================================
@commentId = COMMENT_ID_FROM_PREVIOUS_RESPONSE

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### ============================================
### 10. GET TASK HISTORY (Audit Log)
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with audit log entries

### ============================================
### 11. GET SUBTASKS
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/subtasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with list of subtasks (may be empty)

### ============================================
### 12. AI DECOMPOSE TASK
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/decompose-task
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "taskId": "{{taskId}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with suggested subtasks

### ============================================
### 13. DELETE TASK
### ============================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### ============================================
### 14. VERIFY TASK IS DELETED
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 404 Not Found (soft deleted)

### ============================================
### EDGE CASES TO TEST
### ============================================

### Test 1: Create task with empty tags
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Task with Empty Tags",
  "description": "Testing empty tags array",
  "priority": "Low",
  "category": "Other",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": null,
  "tags": ""
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### Test 2: Create task with multiple tags
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Task with Multiple Tags",
  "description": "Testing multiple tags",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "category": "Development",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": null,
  "tags": "tag1,tag2,tag3,tag4,tag5"
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### Test 3: Create task with all null optional fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Minimal Task",
  "description": "Only required fields",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "category": "Development",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": null,
  "tags": ""
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### Test 4: Try to create task with invalid priority
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid Priority Task",
  "description": "Testing validation",
  "priority": "InvalidPriority",
  "category": "Development",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": null,
  "tags": ""
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request with validation error

### Test 5: Try to create task with missing required field
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title field",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "category": "Development",
  "assignedToUserId": null,
  "dueDate": null,
  "estimatedHours": null,
  "tags": ""
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request with validation error

### ============================================
### PERFORMANCE TESTS
### ============================================

### Test 1: Get tasks with filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&status=InProgress&priority=High&category=Development
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with filtered results

### Test 2: Get tasks with search
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&searchTerm=test
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with search results

### Test 3: Get tasks with date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&dueDateFrom=2026-05-01&dueDateTo=2026-06-30
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK with tasks in date range

